;; Reviewed 2026-10-10 (written by Claude, from the design, Oberon2.pdf,
;; the MACRO manual, LLVM's code generator and the guest runs; for the
;; user's review). Why this is right:
;; - Phase 16 step 3 (section 14): SYSTEM.BYTE is a byte, "B", as CHAR
;;   is. A value BYTE parameter is passed as the calling standard passes a
;;   byte, a longword: a CHAR zero-extended (MOVZBL), a SHORTINT sign-
;;   extended (CVTBL), a constant by MOVL; the callee reads its low byte,
;;   MOVB 4(AP). A VAR BYTE takes the variable's address (MOVAB).
;; - A VAR ARRAY OF SYSTEM.BYTE takes any variable (Oberon2.pdf, Appendix
;;   C), passed as an open array is: its address, then one length, the
;;   variable's size in bytes, as LLVM's: #4 for a LONGINT and for the
;;   record (a CHAR, a byte of padding, a word-aligned INTEGER), #12 for
;;   ARRAY 2, 3 OF INTEGER; for an open array, its lengths multiplied
;;   (MULL2) and then by its element's size, #2.
;; - In Fill, x[n] is a byte: MOVB in index mode, which scales by one,
;;   after the index check against that length.
;; - BytesOut, built by both backends under -O2 and -OC, prints the same
;;   (output.expected) here and on the guest: bytes copied through BYTE
;;   parameters, each byte of an integer, a HUGEINT, a record, a fixed
;;   array, an open one and a two-dimensional one, and arrays filled.
